cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use Prospector in teaching or research, please cite it as below."
title: "Prospector for PyMOL: find, show and explain protein structures by name"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: "Pattofatto"
    given-names: "Lorenzo"
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0008-7977-2084"
    affiliation: "Imperial College London"
version: "2.9.7"
date-released: "2026-11-25"
license: MIT
abstract: >-
  Prospector for PyMOL is an open-source plugin for the molecular viewer PyMOL
  that lets students find, show and explain protein structures by name. A
  protein, gene, UniProt ID or PDB ID typed in plain words is resolved to the
  best experimental structure, with the ranking explained. The plugin then
  explains what is on screen (functional sites, bound molecules, disease
  variants), recolours and redraws on request, shows mutations side by side,
  measures and compares structures, and builds idealised models of DNA, RNA,
  peptides, membranes and micelles alongside real biological assemblies from
  the PDB. Plain-sentence requests are read by built-in rules, with an
  optional AI model (the user's own Anthropic API key) for the rest. Every
  feature is a PyMOL command and a button in a docked panel, and the PyMOL
  commands behind each step can be shown, so the plugin also teaches PyMOL.
repository-code: "https://github.com/lorenzopattofatto10-wq/prospector-for-pymol"
keywords:
  - PyMOL
  - plugin
  - protein structure
  - structural biology
  - education
  - Protein Data Bank
